 typedef struct { int secondary, reduced; } rb_guest_heat_role;
 
+// RewindBox (patch 0335): the thermal guest heuristics run only when asked for (S2A_RB_GUEST_QOS_THERMAL=1). Up to patch 0334 they ran unless the variable said otherwise:
+//   at Fair, 76 to 77 secondary guest threads of Mario Kart World went from USER_INTERACTIVE to USER_INITIATED (patch 0240), and at Serious the secondary pollers slept
+//   longer (patches 0270 and 0282). In the IPA 827 races at Fair no gain was ever measured from the first, neither on the frame (the pool phase after the submit, 2.9 to
+//   4.7 ms with the threads interactive on 18 November against 3.1 to 4.7 ms lowered, different builds) nor on the CPU power (0.78 to 0.96 W whatever the load), while it
+//   lowers the recording threads nx-173 and nx-174 and the threads that wake the submitting one, which the frame waits for; Serious was never reached. Off, the
+//   thermal-state monitor is not installed, so no thread changes class and the Serious delays have no state to start from.
+static inline int rb_guest_qos_thermal_asked(const char *value) { return value && value[0] == '1' && !value[1]; }
+
